Missing optional packages are offered in an interactive multiselect. \`--yes\`, unattended runs, and ordinary dry runs skip them; \`--with-optional\` opts into all of them. \`mise bootstrap packages apply manager:package\` remains the explicit way to install one package.

Missing optionals do not count as drift in status, plan, or doctor, while installed optionals remain managed and protected from prune. OCI builds skip optional packages by default.

*AI-assisted — Tool: Codex; model: OpenAI/GPT-5; version: unavailable.*`;
